  "id": "frohlichs-syndrome",
  "term": "Fröhlich’s syndrome",
  "definition": "Fröhlich’s syndrome is a rare acquired endocrine disorder, more often seen in males, that results from damage to the hypothalamus. It is associated with obesity, short stature, delayed puberty, underdeveloped sexual function, visual problems, and excessive thirst and urination.",
